Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose Dweep 
Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose Dweep, formerly known as Ross Island, is located near Sri Vijaya Puram, South Andaman district. Once the administrative headquarters of the British in the Andamans, it is now a popular tourist spot with historic ruins, scenic beaches, and rich history.

https://tourism.andamannicobar.gov.in/userpages/admin/uploads/heritage/1756086179_IPT_7716.JPG 

Viper Island
Viper Island, located near Sri Vijaya Puram, is a site of immense historical significance. Before the infamous Cellular Jail was constructed, this island housed a women’s prison and gallows where freedom fighters and convicts were incarcerated during British rule.The island derives its name from the HMS Viper, a British ship that wrecked near its shores in the 18th century. Today, Viper Island stands as a symbol of colonial oppression and India’s freedom struggle, while also offering scenic views of the sea and nearby islands.
https://tourism.andamannicobar.gov.in/userpages/admin/uploads/heritage/1756132189_viper1.PNG 

Chatham Island
Chatham Island, located just 3 km from Sri Vijaya Puram and connected by a road bridge, is famous for housing the historic Chatham Saw Mill—one of Asia’s oldest and largest, established in 1883. The island also features a Forest Museum showcasing the rich timber heritage of the Andamans, along with remnants from World War II. Easily accessible by road in about 10–15 minutes from the city, it is a popular stop for visitors exploring Sri Vijaya Puram.
