The Anthropological Museum
The Anthropological Museum, located in Port Blair (South Andaman district, Sri Vijay Puram area), is one of the most informative museums of the islands. It offers a rare and insightful look into the indigenous tribes of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands, their history, lifestyle, art, tools, and culture.

Exhibits: Wooden boats & Canoes used by the Nicobarese and Andamanese tribes.
Hunting & Fishing Equipment – Bows, arrows, harpoons, nets, and traps.
Traditional Clothing & Ornaments – Tribal dresses, jewelry made of shells, bones, and natural fibers.
Household Items – Cooking utensils, storage containers, and handmade tools.
Miniature Huts & Models showing tribal settlements and architecture.
Bones & Skulls – Anthropological studies on ancient inhabitants.
Tribal Paintings & Crafts – Cultural expressions through art and carvings.
Photographic Archives – Old and rare photographs of tribal life and culture.
