The Samudrika Marine Museum
The Samudrika Marine Museum, located in Port Blair, is managed by the Indian Navy. It is one of the most popular museums in the Andaman Islands, designed to create awareness about marine life, ecosystems, tribal communities, and the rich history of the islands. The museum houses an impressive collection of corals, seashells, fish species, marine animals, and tribal artifacts that provide visitors with an in-depth understanding of Andaman’s biodiversity and cultural heritage.

Exhibits:

Corals & Shells – Wide variety of colorful shells and corals from the islands.
Marine Life – Models and preserved specimens of fish, sharks, and other sea creatures.
Tribal Section – Displays on the indigenous tribes of Andaman & Nicobar Islands.
Island Ecosystem – Information on flora, fauna, and natural resources.
Naval History – Insight into the role of the Indian Navy in the region.
