The Zoological Survey of India Museum
The Zoological Survey of India Museum in Port Blair is a must-visit for nature enthusiasts, researchers, and students. It provides an in-depth look into the diverse fauna of the Andaman & Nicobar Islands, featuring preserved specimens of marine life, birds, reptiles, and mammals. The museum is managed by the Zoological Survey of India, which is responsible for surveying and documenting the rich biodiversity of the islands.

Exhibits:

Marine Life – Preserved specimens of fishes, corals, seashells, and other sea creatures.
Bird Collection – Rare endemic bird species found only in the Andamans.
Reptiles – Turtles, crocodiles, and snakes from the island ecosystem.
Crustaceans & Mollusks – Crabs, lobsters, shells, and other marine invertebrates.
Mammals – Specimens and displays of unique mammals inhabiting the islands.
Research Material –Educational resources on the biodiversity and ecological importance of the Andaman & Nicobar region.
